Adds external corroboration of the v1->v4 finding (amortized inference > naive
energy-minimization on an energy/Ising landscape): NVIDIA's open Ising QEC decoder
(2026-04-14, Apache-2.0) is a TINY learned 3D-CNN (~912K/1.79M params) that beats
PyMatching/MWPM — the classical combinatorial energy-minimization decoder for the
surface code — 2.25-2.5x faster + 1.11-1.53x more accurate at d=13. Surface-code
decoding maps to MAP inference on the random-bond Ising model (Dennis-Kitaev-
Landahl-Preskill 2002), so a neural net beating MWPM = amortized-inference >
energy-minimization on an Ising-structured problem, deployed in production QEC.
Answers "is the Sudoku result just a toy?" (no). Honest caveat: the energy/Ising-
inference framing is the physics literature's, NOT NVIDIA's (they give no reason
for the "Ising" name). Naming note: "NVIDIA Ising" (quantum AI) != Ising machines.
See memory nvidia-ising-qec-amortized.

